    "directions": [
      "In a food processor, roughly chop the almonds, walnuts, and hazelnuts together with the powdered sugar. Mix them with the chopped dates, and then the flour.",
      "Beat the egg whites together with the brown sugar and the granulated sugar; add in the dried fruit mixture, then pour everything into a baking pan lined with a buttered and floured sheet of parchment paper.",
      "The baking pan’s edges should be at least 3/4-inch high; you can also use a disposable aluminum tray lined with parchment paper. Bake at 340°F for 40 minutes: do not open the oven while it is baking, otherwise it will sag and collapse. Remove it from the oven and let it cool off a bit; remove the blondie from the tray and let it cool completely on a grate, then cut it into squares."
    ],
